<title>CANADA: RUGBY UNION-ARGENTINA, CANADA WIN OPENING PAN AM GAMES.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-ARGENTINA, CANADA WIN OPENING PAN AM GAMES.</headline>
<dateline>NEPEAN, Ontario 1996-09-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina beat the</p>
<p>United States 29-26 (halftime 11-6), and Canada defeated</p>
<p>Uruguay 24-18 (halftime 18-5) in the opening games of the</p>
<p>four-nation Pan American tournament on Saturday.</p>
<p>Argentina 29  United States 26</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Argentina - Tries: Roberto Travaglini, Octavio Bartolucki,</p>
<p>Eduardo Simone. Conversions: Santiago Maison. Penalties:</p>
<p>Maison (2), Gonzalo quesada (2)</p>
<p>United States - Tries: Alec Parker, Andre Bachelet.</p>
<p>Conversions: Matt Alexander (2). Penalties: Alexander (4).</p>
<p>Canada 24  Uruguay 18</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Canada - Tries: Kevin Wirachowski, Jason Penaluna.</p>
<p>Conversions: Bob Ross. Penalties: Bob Ross (4)</p>
<p>Uruguay - Tries: Antonio Dabbo, Marcello Calandra.</p>
<p>Conversions: Diego Aguirre. Penalties: Aguirre. Drop goals:</p>
<p>Santiago Silva.</p>
</text>
